From 305bf06fe62264a673351106aebe09e01b3ac4e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:17:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Win bonus, rotation penalty, and a points breakdown for every
 score

Scoring (v2 match days, from 19 Nov 2026)
- Winning team: +3 to each player on the side that wins (rolling subs
  included); the floater gets +2 when there's a winner; draw or an
  abandoned "no result" match gives no bonus. Decided from the goal log.
- Missed rotation: -2 to a player who skipped their GK or sub stint, which
  flows to every selector who picked them.
- matchItems() itemises every point with a reason; scoreMatch() now totals
  those items, so breakdowns always add up to the tables.

Scorekeeper
- "No result" switch and live "White win / Draw" label under the score.
- Fair play and rotation merged into one Conduct checklist per player
  (both ticked by default; unticking asks why), with "Mark all rotated".
- Publishing requires "I've checked who went in goal and who subbed".
- Points preview shows each player's itemised chips.

Users
- Pick 7 table rows expand (lazy GET /api/pick7/breakdown/[id]) into a
  "where the points came from" bar by source plus every round, each pick
  itemised (goal, assist, win, MOTM, fair play, rotation) with tooltips,
  "Didn't play" lines, and a note when a scorecard was corrected.
- Same breakdown in My season on My Team; match report gains Win and Rot
  columns plus result and missed-rotation lines; rules, table and home
  pages list the new values.

Tests: 93 (8 new in lib/league/winRotation.test.ts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PtuBR2yKPy8UddCaB5RWRB
